  "notes": [
    "client is the line of the HttpClient call (GetFromJsonAsync, PostAsJsonAsync, SendAsync). Most URLs are interpolated a line above from a remoteServiceBaseUrl field; the path is the field plus the literal suffix, with the query string dropped.",
    "server is the line of the Map<Verb>( call in the minimal API group.",
    "WebAppComponents/Services/CatalogService.cs is a shared-library class registered as a typed client only by WebApp, so its calls belong to webapp. HybridApp has its own CatalogService.",
    "Catalog.API is versioned by the api-version query parameter. WebApp's catalog client adds api-version=2.0 (AddApiVersion(2.0)), so GET /items and /items/withsemanticrelevance resolve to the v2 handlers, not the v1 ones.",
    "ASP.NET Core route matching is case-insensitive: catalogBrands matches /catalogbrands, catalogTypes /catalogtypes, and /api/Orders/ the api/orders group.",
    "OrderingService.CreateOrder posts through new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Post, remoteServiceBaseUrl) and SendAsync; the client line is the SendAsync line."
  ]
